import ShielddGnarkFormal.Poseidon6Bridge

/-! Reusable deployed-slice ⇒ `permSpec6` link for width-6 Poseidon classes
(note_commitment, nullifier, statement.hash, compress_to_field).

The deployed flat slice reconstructs every S-box output as `Poseidon6Bridge.p17 (LC)`
(via the per-class `*DeployedBridge` reconstruction). These generic round equations
turn each `fr7`/`pr7` into a flat MDS-of-wires vector, so a deployed evaluator can be
composed up to `permSpec6` round-by-round without unrolling the partial-round linear
lanes (which would blow up — CLAUDE ≤60-gate rule). Proved once, reused per round. -/

